For each word below, write ONE short sentence (12 to 22 words) that uses the word itself, spelled in full, in the sense given. Give it voice and mood: a question, someone speaking, a sigh, delight, a warning. No definitions; show the word in a moment of life. Answer as one JSON object mapping each WORD (as given, upper case) to its sentence. JSON only.

MARKER: some conspicuous object used to distinguish or mark something.
MASS: the property of a body that causes it to have weight in a gravitational field.
MATRIX: (mathematics) a rectangular array of quantities or expressions set out by rows and columns.
MEASURE: any maneuver made as part of progress toward a goal.
MEMBER: one of the persons who compose a social group (especially individuals who have joined and participate in a group organization).
MESH: the number of openings per linear inch of a screen.
